<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Turk Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grand Turk Island is the main island of the Turks Islands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and seat of government of the Turks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caicos-islands">Caicos Islands</a>. From the late 17th century Bermudian salt rakers worked its salt ponds, and its merchants' resentment of taxes levied from Nassau led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to separate the islands from the Bahamas in 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-turk-island.jpg" alt="Grand Turk Island" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drdread66 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Turk_from_the_air.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
